### ISP-1

A deferred link carries its text, strips the mark and opens nothing: the target document contributes no headings.

```console
$ grep -n "Claude" full.bundle.md
27:- If you are Claude, compile [Claude](rules/claude.md).

$ grep -c "^# Claude Rules" full.bundle.md
0

[exit 1: grep, not pf — 1 means no line matched]
```

### ISP-2

A dispatched link withholds its target exactly as a deferral does and publishes its mark, because the mark states who compiles the slot.

```console
$ grep -n "Record Delivery" plan.bundle.md
10:2. Delegate delivery to [» Record Delivery](artifacts/delivery.md).

$ grep -c "^# Record Delivery" plan.bundle.md
0

[exit 1: grep, not pf — 1 means no line matched]
```

### ISP-3

stdout is the bundle alone and the entry destinations go to stderr as data, so a wrapper reads them without scraping Markdown.

```console
$ pf -o - modes/plan.md 2>/dev/null
# Plan Mode

Scopes work.

Follow [Procedure](#procedure). The other sections are material that procedure references.

## Procedure

1. Follow [the link rule](#check-every-link).
2. Delegate delivery to [» Record Delivery](artifacts/delivery.md).

## Outcomes

- A scoped plan.

# Rules

## Check Every Link

- Check every link.

[exit 0]
```

### ISP-4

A withheld target that does not exist is refused, because a dispatch an agent will follow is one that can succeed.

```console
$ pf -c modes/missing.md
E_TARGET_NOT_FOUND: the reference '../artifacts/gone.md' names no document under the allowed source root
  reference: ../artifacts/gone.md
  source: modes/missing.md:11
  chain: modes/missing.md → artifacts/gone.md
  remedy: name a document the source root carries

[exit 1]
```

### ISP-5

A consumer carries a document it never names, reached through one it does, so segregation cannot be enforced from outside the consumer.

```console
$ grep -n "Agents" modes/full.md
(no output above: full.md never names agents.md)

$ grep -c "^### Agents" full.bundle.md
2

[exit 0: grep, not pf — 1 means no line matched]
```

### DIP-1a

Over a closure of compiled links the bundle is independent of the working directory, because every root is declared by its source. No output below is the observation.

```console
$ diff compiled-skill.bundle.md compiled-parent.bundle.md

[exit 0: diff, not pf — 0 means the files agree]
```

### DIP-1b

Over a closure holding withheld links, only those destinations move, because a withheld destination is deliberately working-directory-relative so a later invocation can be handed it.

```console
$ diff full-skill.bundle.md full-parent.bundle.md
27,28c27,28
< - If you are Claude, compile [Claude](skill/rules/claude.md).
< - If you are Codex, compile [Codex](skill/rules/codex.md).
---
> - If you are Claude, compile [Claude](rules/claude.md).
> - If you are Codex, compile [Codex](rules/codex.md).

[exit 1: diff, not pf — 0 means the files agree]
```

### DIP-2

The caller cannot retarget a dependency root: structure is source-owned and only operational flags are the caller's.

```console
$ pf -o - modes/plan.md -r .
E_INVALID_USAGE: unrecognized arguments: -r .
  remedy: run pf -h for usage

[exit 2]
```

### DIP-3

The caller cannot retarget a group for the same reason.

```console
$ pf -o - modes/plan.md -g other
E_INVALID_USAGE: unrecognized arguments: -g other
  remedy: run pf -h for usage

[exit 2]
```

